„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿For thus saith the LORD touching Shallum the son of Josiah king of Judah, which reigned instead of Josiah his father, which went forth out of this place; He shall not return thither any more:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙabut he shall die in the place whither they have led him captive, and shall see this land no more.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦Woe unto him that buildeth his house by unrighteousness, and his chambers by wrong; that useth his neighbour's service without wages, and giveth him not for his work;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’that saith, I will build me a wide house and large chambers, and cutteth him out windows; and it is cieled with cedar, and painted with vermilion.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–Shalt thou reign, because thou closest thyself in cedar? did not thy father eat and drink, and do judgment and justice, and then it was well with him?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnHe judged the cause of the poor and needy; then it was well with him: was not this to know me? saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut thine eyes and thine heart are not but for thy covetousness, and for to shed innocent blood, and for oppression, and for violence, to do it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÚTherefore thus saith the LORD concerning Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah; They shall not lament for him, saying, Ah my brother! or, Ah sister! they shall not lament for him, saying, Ah lord! or, Ah his glory!¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaHe shall be buried with the burial of an ass, drawn and cast forth beyond the gates of Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxGo up to Lebanon, and cry; and lift up thy voice in Bashan, and cry from the passages: for all thy lovers are destroyed.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘I spake unto thee in thy prosperity; but thou saidst, I will not hear. This hath been thy manner from thy youth, that thou obeyedst not my voice.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—The wind shall eat up all thy pastors, and thy lovers shall go into captivity: surely then shalt thou be ashamed and confounded for all thy wickedness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•O inhabitant of Lebanon, that makest thy nest in the cedars, how gracious shalt thou be when pangs come upon thee, the pain as of a woman in travail!¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAs I live, saith the LORD, though Coniah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah were the signet upon my right hand, yet would I pluck thee thence;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙËand I will give thee into the hand of them that seek thy life, and into the hand of them whose face thou fearest, even into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and into the hand of the Chaldeans.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~And I will cast thee out, and thy mother that bare thee, into another country, where ye were not born; and there shall ye die.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOBut to the land whereunto they desire to return, thither shall they not return.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­Is this man Coniah a despised broken idol? is he a vessel wherein is no pleasure? wherefore are they cast out, he and his seed, and are cast into a land which they know not?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ1O earth, earth, earth, hear the word of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁThus saith the LORD, Write ye this man childless, a man that shall not prosper in his days: for no man of his seed shall prosper, sitting upon the throne of David, and ruling any more in Judah.¦layout ªlast_verse